<<~ ahu slot=`#/addendum-blocker-2-cured-under-the-seat-s-ruling`>>

!! Addendum: blocker 2 cured under the seat's ruling (b)

The lane head is ''ecb26d4d0'', pushed. The red is `99b89f50b` and the cure is `ecb26d4d0`.

* ''The red.'' `packages/lararium-node/tests/p27-leaf-absence.test.ts` runs over the browser-shaped readers (no face catalog, `faceOwns` read off the sealed map). Before the cure, a leaf face plane asking for sibling `fleet` refused. After the cure it passes. A companion check shows the same plane still withholds from `world`.
* ''Control 1.'' A leaf plane whose own carrier declares VEIL still refuses `fleet` (`declared-tier-audience`).
* ''Control 2.'' The node keeps its real registry: it still refuses `secrets-registry-unread` until its catalog binds.
* ''Control 3.'' An improvised absence plane, anything other than the one constant, refuses with `secrets-absence-unestablished`.
* ''The cure.'' `makeHeldShareFloor` now takes a named secrets source:
** the node passes `secrets: { catalog }` (typed `HeldShareFloor<SecretsRegistry>`);
** a surface passes `secrets: { establishedAbsence: NO_CONTRACT_SECRETS_PLANE }` (`HeldShareFloor<null>`).

`open-browser-vessel.ts` composes the absence and drops the dead `shareCatalog` cell.
* ''Canon.'' `cap-tier#/the-keystone` names the ruling and cites `stable-founding-road#/rulings` (the stories' leans of 2026-11-07, item 5, and "a page never stands as a vessel", 2026-10-29). The carrier is resealed.
* ''Checks.'' The P27 manifest, 56 node and mesh files, passes with each file run alone in bwrap. The pre-push gate is green. The browser-runner files ride CI. I added no new browser-runner witness; the node test over the browser-shaped readers carries the red.

<<~/ahu>>

